(six `fields` keys: NO `duedate`, the slot Q-ANSWERS Q6's default). **The ADF of a text** (by program; the project's `adf_doc` of `b1785.py` builds it from a list of paragraphs): split the filled text on `\n\n`; each block is ONE `paragraph` holding ONE `text` node (every block of these texts is one line; no `>` block, no marks). **The inverse** for the read-back: the reader's `adf_paras` (each paragraph's text nodes joined), the list EQUAL to the blocks; never `adf_text` of the whole body (it joins with no separator). Expect HTTP 201 and a key `OXPD2-<n>`; write `{"kind": "create", "t": "T-A7", "key": <key>, "clock": <date>}` to the write log at once; then GET `issue/<key>?fields=summary,description,assignee,duedate,labels,issuelinks,issuetype,status,project,attachment` and check: summary EQUAL to A7-S; the paragraphs EQUAL to the filled A7-D's blocks; assignee `616503d4bfa2c1006b1971d1`; duedate null; labels exactly `["oxpd-kamil-action"]`; issue type `10030`; project `OXPD2`; exactly one issue link, type `10003`, to OXPD2-1; 0 attachments; a one-character mutant of the summary UNEQUAL (control). Write `{"kind": "verify-create", ...}`.
